WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.192
Many local inference servers provide an A P I that follows the same general shape as familiar chat-completions

00:00:08.192 --> 00:00:16.412
interfaces. This lets application code send messages over H T T P while the server handles model loading and generation.

00:00:16.412 --> 00:00:20.447
It also makes it easier to replace the inference engine later.

00:00:20.447 --> 00:00:26.942
That compatibility can make application code portable because the client interface stays similar even when the

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:29.713
underlying local model changes.
